## Limits and next boundary

New no-testable completion, record publication, cleanup/resume and finalized rejection/materialized-invalid branches remain statically reviewed only until a separately authorized real campaign. Exact-duplicate-with-nonempty-template-changes remains a known fail-closed incompatibility requiring an architect decision before that form can publish. Lifecycle completion does not count as an evaluated experiment or establish a promotable champion. Two real evaluated feedback rounds with critic/checkpoint/cleanup evidence remain required.

B4c summary counts/labels, bounded rejection metrics in investigator requests and detailed feedback/history exposition were not changed. No tests were read, created, changed or run. No synthetic probes/events/records/fixtures/responses, model/API calls, credential reads, candidate evaluation, campaign launch/resume/poll, runtime evidence writes, evaluator rebuild, commits, pushes or deployment occurred. This checkpoint grants no additional call or campaign budget.
